{"name":"Avocado Pear","hex":"#555337","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"avocado pear","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fruit of the avocado tree; an avocado."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/avocado_pear"}],"entries":[{"title":"Avocado","blocks":[{"text":"The avocado, alligator pear or avocado pear is an evergreen tree in the laurel family (Lauraceae). It is native to the Americas, with archaeological evidence of early human avocado use dating back thousands of years across various regions of Central and South America. It was prized for its large and unusually oily fruit. The native range of avocado extends from Mexico to Peru, encompassing much of Central America and parts of northern and western South America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Persea_americana_fruit_2.JPG/330px-Persea_americana_fruit_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avocado"},{"title":"Pear","blocks":[{"text":"Pears are a genus of trees, Pyrus, in the family Rosaceae, that bear an edible apple-like fruit of the same name. Several species of pears are cultivated for their fruit and juices, while others are grown as ornamental flowering trees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Pears.jpg/330px-Pears.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pear"},{"title":"Shades of chartreuse","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of chartreuse are listed below. Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green, so named because of its resemblance to the color of the French liqueur green chartreuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg/330px-Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_chartreuse"},{"title":"Shades of yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color yellow may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a yellow or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Color_icon_yellow.svg/330px-Color_icon_yellow.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Avocado_Hass_-_single_and_halved.jpg/500px-Avocado_Hass_-_single_and_halved.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Avocado_Hass_-_single_and_halved.jpg/1280px-Avocado_Hass_-_single_and_halved.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Avocado_Hass_-_single_and_halved.jpg/500px-Avocado_Hass_-_single_and_halved.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAvocado_Hass_-_single_and_halved.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Flower_of_Avocado_2.jpg/500px-Flower_of_Avocado_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Flower_of_Avocado_2.jpg/1280px-Flower_of_Avocado_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Flower_of_Avocado_2.jpg/500px-Flower_of_Avocado_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Avocado flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F